package pane:extension@0.1.0;

// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
//
// Preferences: typed values a package's `pane.json` declares under
// `preferences`, for the whole extension or for one command, and the user
// sets in Pane: on the Setup screen before the command's first run, and on
// the extension's card in Settings › Extensions. Pane stores them (a
// password as a local credential, every other value as an extension
// setting); a command only reads them. Rust commands read them through
// pane-guest (`pane_guest::preferences::values`, deserialized with serde),
// JavaScript and TypeScript ones through `@pane/extension/preferences`
// (`getPreferenceValues`). The header follows `package`: comments above it
// would document the package, which extension.wit already does.

/// Reading the command's effective preference values.
interface preferences {
  /// The effective preference values of the command `command` (its id in
  /// `pane.json`) of the caller's own package, as a JSON object: the
  /// package's preferences, then the command's own, each name to the value
  /// the user set or else its declared default. A checkbox's value is a
  /// boolean (`false` while it has none), every other kind's text (a
  /// dropdown's, the chosen option's `value`; a file's, folder's or
  /// application's, its path). A preference with no value and no default is
  /// left out. A stored value that no longer fits (a dropdown option no
  /// longer declared, a file or folder that no longer exists) counts as
  /// none.
  ///
  /// With `command` none: the command Pane is running in this component
  /// (the one it opened, ran or asked), or else the only command the
  /// component serves. A component serving several commands names the
  /// command in calls Pane makes for no command in particular, such as its
  /// root results.
  ///
  /// Refused, with the reason, for a command built into Pane, a command
  /// the package does not have, or code that is stopped (its package was
  /// disabled, reloaded, updated or uninstalled).
  values: func(command: option<string>) -> result<string, string>;
}

/// The preferences import alone, for guest bindings.
world preferences-user {
  import preferences;
}
